[
{:name "Account-Based Marketing (ABM)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/account-based-marketing" :description "Account-based marketing (ABM) targets a defined list of high-value companies with coordinated sales and marketing. Learn how ABM works in B2B."}
{:name "Account Executive (AE)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/account-executive" :description "An account executive (AE) is the seller who runs qualified deals from discovery to signed contract. Learn what an AE does and how it differs from SDRs."}
{:name "Agentic Workflow" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/agentic-workflow" :description "An agentic workflow is a multi-step process where AI agents plan, use tools and make decisions within defined steps. Learn how it differs from automation."}
{:name "AI Agent" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/ai-agent" :description "An AI agent is software built on a language model that plans steps and uses tools to complete a goal. Learn how AI agents are used in sales and marketing."}
{:name "AI Sales Agent" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/ai-sales-agent" :description "An AI sales agent is AI software that carries out sales tasks such as research, outreach and follow-up with some autonomy. Learn what they do and their limits."}
{:name "AI SDR" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/ai-sdr" :description "An AI SDR is software that uses AI to research prospects, write outreach and handle replies. Learn what AI SDRs do and how they differ from a sequencer."}
{:name "Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/annual-recurring-revenue" :description "Annual recurring revenue (ARR) is the yearly value of a company's subscription contracts. Learn how ARR is calculated and how it differs from revenue."}
{:name "Attribution Model" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/attribution-model" :description "An attribution model is the rule for giving credit for a conversion to the touchpoints before it. Learn first-touch, last-touch and multi-touch models."}
{:name "Average Contract Value (ACV)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/average-contract-value" :description "Average contract value (ACV) is the typical yearly value of a customer contract. Learn how ACV is calculated and why it shapes a go-to-market motion."}
{:name "B2B SaaS" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/b2b-saas" :description "B2B SaaS is software sold to businesses as a subscription and delivered over the internet. Learn how the B2B SaaS model works and what it measures."}
{:name "Backlinks" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/backlinks" :description "Backlinks are links from other websites to yours. Learn why backlinks matter for SEO, what makes a good one and how dofollow and nofollow links differ."}
{:name "Bottom of Funnel (BOFU)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/bottom-of-funnel" :description "Bottom of funnel (BOFU) is the decision stage, where buyers choose a vendor. Learn what BOFU content looks like and why it converts best."}
{:name "Bounce Rate" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/bounce-rate" :description "Bounce rate is the share of website sessions that leave without engaging further. Learn how it is measured and how it differs from email bounce rate."}
{:name "Business Development Representative (BDR)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/business-development-representative" :description "A business development representative (BDR) prospects new accounts through outbound outreach and books sales meetings. Learn how a BDR differs from an SDR."}
{:name "Buyer Persona" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/buyer-persona" :description "A buyer persona is a profile of the person who buys or influences a purchase. Learn how B2B buyer personas differ from an ICP and how they shape outreach."}
{:name "Buying Signals" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/buying-signals" :description "Buying signals are events and behaviors that suggest a company may need a product soon, such as funding or hiring. Learn how B2B teams use buying signals."}
{:name "Channel Partner" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/channel-partner" :description "A channel partner is a company that sells, resells or recommends another company's product to its own customers. Learn the main partner types."}
{:name "Churn Rate" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/churn-rate" :description "Churn rate is the share of customers or revenue lost in a period. Learn how customer churn and revenue churn are calculated and why they differ."}
{:name "Cold Calling" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/cold-calling" :description "Cold calling is phoning a potential buyer who has had no prior contact with the seller. Learn how B2B cold calling works and where it fits in outbound."}
{:name "Cold Email" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/cold-email" :description "Cold email is a first, unsolicited email sent to a potential buyer with no prior relationship. Learn how B2B cold email works and what it depends on."}
{:name "Competitive Intelligence" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/competitive-intelligence" :description "Competitive intelligence is gathering and analyzing public information about competitors to make better decisions. Learn how sales and marketing use it."}
{:name "Content Marketing" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/content-marketing" :description "Content marketing is creating useful content that attracts and keeps a defined audience. Learn how B2B content marketing works and how it is measured."}
{:name "Context Engineering" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/context-engineering" :description "Context engineering is designing everything a language model sees: instructions, examples, data, tool output and memory. Learn how it differs from prompts."}
{:name "Conversion Rate" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/conversion-rate" :description "Conversion rate is the share of visitors or leads who complete a desired action. Learn the formula and how B2B teams use it across the funnel."}
{:name "Conversion Rate Optimization (CRO)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/conversion-rate-optimization" :description "Conversion rate optimization (CRO) is the practice of raising the share of visitors who take a desired action. Learn how CRO testing works."}
{:name "CRM (Customer Relationship Management)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/crm" :description "A CRM is the system where a company records its contacts, accounts, deals and every sales and marketing interaction. Learn what a CRM does in B2B."}
{:name "Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/customer-acquisition-cost" :description "Customer acquisition cost (CAC) is the total sales and marketing spend needed to win one new customer. Learn the CAC formula and how B2B teams use it."}
{:name "Customer Lifetime Value (CLV)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/customer-lifetime-value" :description "Customer lifetime value (CLV or LTV) is the total value a customer brings over their relationship with a company. Learn how CLV is calculated and used."}
{:name "Data Enrichment" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/data-enrichment" :description "Data enrichment adds missing details such as emails, titles and company size to your records from external sources. Learn how B2B data enrichment works."}
{:name "Data Hygiene" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/data-hygiene" :description "Data hygiene is keeping CRM and marketing data accurate, complete and free of duplicates. Learn why B2B data decays and how teams keep it clean."}
{:name "Deduplication (Dedupe)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/deduplication" :description "Deduplication (dedupe) finds records that describe the same person or company and merges them. Learn how dedupe works in CRM data and list building."}
{:name "Demand Generation" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/demand-generation" :description "Demand generation builds awareness and interest in a target market before buyers are ready to buy. Learn how it differs from lead generation."}
{:name "Discovery Call" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/discovery-call" :description "A discovery call is an early sales conversation to understand a prospect's situation, problems and buying process. Learn what a discovery call covers."}
{:name "DKIM" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/dkim" :description "DKIM (DomainKeys Identified Mail) adds a cryptographic signature to outgoing email so receivers can verify the sending domain. Learn how DKIM works."}
{:name "DMARC" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/dmarc" :description "DMARC is an email authentication policy that tells receiving servers how to handle mail failing SPF or DKIM checks. Learn how DMARC protects a domain."}
{:name "Domain Authority" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/domain-authority" :description "Domain authority is a third-party score that estimates how well a website may rank based on its links. Learn what it measures and its limits."}
{:name "Email Bounce" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/email-bounce" :description "An email bounce is a message that could not be delivered and was returned. Learn the difference between hard and soft bounces and why bounce rate matters."}
{:name "Email Deliverability" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/email-deliverability" :description "Email deliverability is whether your email reaches the inbox instead of spam. Learn how authentication and sender reputation affect cold email."}
{:name "Email Finder" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/email-finder" :description "An email finder is a tool that finds a person's likely work email from their name and company. Learn how email finders work and why verification matters."}
{:name "Email Verification" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/email-verification" :description "Email verification checks whether an address exists and can receive mail before you send to it. Learn how email verification protects deliverability."}
{:name "Email Warmup" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/email-warmup" :description "Email warmup is the practice of gradually raising sending volume from a new mailbox or domain to build sender reputation for cold email."}
{:name "Firmographics" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/firmographics" :description "Firmographics are company attributes such as industry, headcount, revenue and location. Learn how B2B teams use firmographic data to segment accounts."}
{:name "First-Party Data" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/first-party-data" :description "First-party data is information a company collects directly from its own audience and customers. Learn how it differs from second- and third-party data."}
{:name "Generative Engine Optimization (GEO)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/generative-engine-optimization" :description "Generative engine optimization (GEO) is shaping content so AI search tools and assistants cite it in their answers. Learn how GEO differs from SEO."}
{:name "Go-to-Market (GTM)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/go-to-market" :description "Go-to-market (GTM) is the plan for how a company reaches buyers, sells to them and wins customers. Learn the parts of a B2B GTM strategy and motion."}
{:name "GTM Engineering" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/gtm-engineering" :description "GTM engineering is building automated go-to-market systems with code, APIs and AI: data, enrichment, signals, outreach and CRM sync. Learn what it covers."}
{:name "Hyper-Personalization" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/hyper-personalization" :description "Hyper-personalization is tailoring each message to the individual recipient using specific research. Learn how it differs from basic personalization."}
{:name "Ideal Customer Profile (ICP)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/ideal-customer-profile" :description "An ideal customer profile (ICP) describes the companies that get the most from your product. Learn how to build one and how it differs from a persona."}
{:name "Inbound Lead" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/inbound-lead" :description "An inbound lead is a potential buyer who contacts a company or shares details on their own initiative. Learn how inbound leads differ from outbound."}
{:name "Intent Data" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/intent-data" :description "Intent data shows which companies are researching a topic and may be moving toward a purchase. Learn first, second and third-party intent."}
{:name "Keyword Research" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/keyword-research" :description "Keyword research is finding the words buyers type into search engines and judging which ones to target. Learn how it works for B2B content and SEO."}
{:name "Landing Page" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/landing-page" :description "A landing page is a web page built for one campaign and one action, such as a demo request. Learn how landing pages differ from home pages."}
{:name "Large Language Model (LLM)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/large-language-model" :description "A large language model (LLM) is an AI model trained on large amounts of text to understand and generate language. Learn how LLMs are used in GTM."}
{:name "Lead Generation" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/lead-generation" :description "Lead generation is the process of finding and attracting potential buyers and capturing their contact details. Learn how B2B lead generation works."}
{:name "Lead Magnet" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/lead-magnet" :description "A lead magnet is a free resource offered in exchange for contact details. Learn how B2B teams use lead magnets on LinkedIn and websites to capture leads."}
{:name "Lead Nurturing" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/lead-nurturing" :description "Lead nurturing is building a relationship with leads who are not ready to buy yet. Learn how B2B nurture sequences work and what they contain."}
{:name "Lead Qualification" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/lead-qualification" :description "Lead qualification is deciding whether a lead is worth pursuing, based on fit, need and timing. Learn common criteria and frameworks such as BANT."}
{:name "Lead Scoring" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/lead-scoring" :description "Lead scoring ranks leads by fit and engagement so sales works the best ones first. Learn how fit and behavior scores work and how lead scoring sets MQLs."}
{:name "LinkedIn Ads" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/linkedin-ads" :description "LinkedIn Ads are paid placements on LinkedIn targeted by job, company and audience data. Learn the main ad formats and how B2B teams use them."}
{:name "LinkedIn InMail" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/linkedin-inmail" :description "LinkedIn InMail lets you message LinkedIn members you are not connected with, using credits from a premium plan. Learn how InMail works in B2B outreach."}
{:name "LinkedIn Sales Navigator" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/linkedin-sales-navigator" :description "LinkedIn Sales Navigator is LinkedIn's paid tool for sales prospecting, with advanced search, lead lists and alerts. Learn what it is used for."}
{:name "LinkedIn Thought Leader Ads" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/linkedin-thought-leader-ads" :description "LinkedIn Thought Leader Ads let a company promote posts written by its people as paid ads. Learn how they work and why B2B teams use them."}
{:name "llms.txt" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/llms-txt" :description "llms.txt is a proposed Markdown file at a website's root that gives AI agents a short overview and links to key content. Learn the format and its purpose."}
{:name "Long-Tail Keywords" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/long-tail-keywords" :description "Long-tail keywords are longer, more specific search phrases with lower volume and clearer intent. Learn why B2B teams target them and how to find them."}
{:name "Lookalike Audience" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/lookalike-audience" :description "A lookalike audience is a group an ad platform builds to resemble a seed list, such as current customers. Learn how B2B teams use lookalikes."}
{:name "Marketing Automation" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/marketing-automation" :description "Marketing automation is software that runs repetitive marketing tasks such as emails, lead scoring and routing on rules. Learn how B2B teams use it."}
{:name "Marketing Qualified Lead (MQL)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/marketing-qualified-lead" :description "A marketing qualified lead (MQL) is a lead that meets marketing's fit and engagement criteria and is ready for sales. Learn how MQLs differ from SQLs."}
{:name "Middle of Funnel (MOFU)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/middle-of-funnel" :description "Middle of funnel (MOFU) is the consideration stage, where buyers research ways to solve a problem. Learn what MOFU content and metrics look like."}
{:name "Model Context Protocol (MCP)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/model-context-protocol" :description "The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard for connecting AI applications to external tools and data. Learn how MCP servers and clients work."}
{:name "Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/monthly-recurring-revenue" :description "Monthly recurring revenue (MRR) is the predictable subscription revenue a company earns each month. Learn how MRR is calculated and its parts."}
{:name "Multi-Touch Attribution" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/multi-touch-attribution" :description "Multi-touch attribution splits credit for a conversion across several touchpoints. Learn the common models and the limits of multi-touch attribution."}
{:name "MX Record" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/mx-record" :description "An MX record is the DNS entry that tells sending servers where to deliver email for a domain. Learn how MX records work and why they matter for cold email."}
{:name "Net Revenue Retention (NRR)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/net-revenue-retention" :description "Net revenue retention (NRR) measures how much recurring revenue a company keeps and grows from existing customers. Learn the NRR formula and its meaning."}
{:name "Outbound Sales" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/outbound-sales" :description "Outbound sales is when the seller starts the conversation with buyers who have not reached out. Learn how outbound differs from inbound and what it uses."}
{:name "Paid Media" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/paid-media" :description "Paid media is any marketing channel where a company pays for placement, such as search, social and display ads. Learn how B2B teams use paid media."}
{:name "Personal Branding" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/personal-branding" :description "Personal branding is how a professional builds a reputation for specific expertise. Learn how founders and B2B leaders use it on LinkedIn."}
{:name "Pipeline Generation" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/pipeline-generation" :description "Pipeline generation is creating qualified sales opportunities that can turn into revenue. Learn how B2B teams build and measure pipeline generation."}
{:name "Product-Led Growth (PLG)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/product-led-growth" :description "Product-led growth (PLG) is a go-to-market motion where the product itself drives signups, adoption and expansion. Learn how PLG works in B2B software."}
{:name "Programmatic SEO" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/programmatic-seo" :description "Programmatic SEO is building many search-targeted pages from a template and a dataset. Learn when it works and how to keep the pages useful."}
{:name "Prompt Engineering" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/prompt-engineering" :description "Prompt engineering is writing and refining instructions so an AI model produces useful, reliable output. Learn the basics and how it fits with context."}
{:name "Reverse IP Lookup" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/reverse-ip-lookup" :description "Reverse IP lookup matches an IP address to the domain or organization behind it. Learn how B2B teams use it to identify companies visiting their site."}
{:name "RevOps (Revenue Operations)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/revops" :description "RevOps (revenue operations) runs the systems, data and processes behind marketing, sales and customer success as one function. Learn what RevOps teams own."}
{:name "Sales Cycle" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-cycle" :description "A sales cycle is the series of steps and the time it takes to turn a prospect into a customer. Learn how B2B teams measure sales cycle length."}
{:name "Sales Development Representative (SDR)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-development-representative" :description "A sales development representative (SDR) prospects and qualifies leads, then books meetings for account executives. Learn what an SDR does in B2B sales."}
{:name "Sales Engagement Platform" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-engagement-platform" :description "A sales engagement platform runs multi-step outreach sequences across email, calls and LinkedIn and tracks the results. Learn what these tools do."}
{:name "Sales Forecast" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-forecast" :description "A sales forecast is an estimate of the revenue a team expects to close in a period. Learn common forecasting methods and how forecast accuracy is judged."}
{:name "Sales Lead" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-lead" :description "A sales lead is a person or company that may become a customer. Learn how leads differ from prospects and opportunities, and the main lead stages."}
{:name "Sales Pipeline" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-pipeline" :description "A sales pipeline is the set of open deals organized by stage, from first meeting to closed. Learn how pipeline stages work and how teams manage them."}
{:name "Sales Playbook" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-playbook" :description "A sales playbook is a written guide to how a team sells: who it targets, what it says and how deals progress. Learn what a sales playbook contains."}
{:name "Sales Prospecting" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-prospecting" :description "Sales prospecting is finding and contacting potential buyers who fit your ideal customer profile. Learn the main prospecting methods in B2B sales."}
{:name "Sales Qualified Lead (SQL)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-qualified-lead" :description "A sales qualified lead (SQL) is a prospect sales has reviewed and accepted as a real opportunity. Learn how SQLs differ from MQLs."}
{:name "Win Rate" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/sales-win-rate" :description "Win rate is the share of sales opportunities that end in a closed won deal. Learn how to calculate win rate and how win-loss analysis improves it."}
{:name "Search Engine Optimization (SEO)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/search-engine-optimization" :description "Search engine optimization (SEO) is improving a website so it ranks in unpaid search results. Learn the main parts of SEO and how it relates to GEO."}
{:name "Search Intent" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/search-intent" :description "Search intent is the goal behind a search query. Learn the four common types of search intent and why matching it matters for SEO and content."}
{:name "Serviceable Addressable Market (SAM)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/serviceable-addressable-market" :description "Serviceable addressable market (SAM) is the part of the total market a company can actually serve today. Learn how SAM relates to TAM and SOM."}
{:name "Social Listening" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/social-listening" :description "Social listening monitors social platforms and communities for mentions of a brand, competitor or topic. Learn how B2B teams turn it into timely outreach."}
{:name "Social Selling" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/social-selling" :description "Social selling is using social networks, mainly LinkedIn, to find, understand and build relationships with buyers. Learn how B2B social selling works."}
{:name "Speed to Lead" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/speed-to-lead" :description "Speed to lead is how quickly a company responds after a lead raises their hand. Learn why response time matters and how teams shorten it."}
{:name "SPF Record" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/spf-record" :description "An SPF record is a DNS TXT record listing the servers allowed to send email for a domain. Learn how SPF checks work and affect cold email delivery."}
{:name "Spintax" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/spintax" :description "Spintax is a text format like {Hi|Hello} that lets sending tools vary a message for each recipient. Learn how spintax works in cold email."}
{:name "Stakeholder Mapping" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/stakeholder-mapping" :description "Stakeholder mapping identifies everyone involved in a B2B purchase and their role and influence. Learn how sales teams map buying committees."}
{:name "Technographics" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/technographics" :description "Technographics describe the software and technologies a company uses. Learn how B2B teams use technographic data to segment and prioritize accounts."}
{:name "Third-Party Data" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/third-party-data" :description "Third-party data is information collected by outside providers and sold or licensed to companies. Learn how B2B teams use it and what to check."}
{:name "Top of Funnel (TOFU)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/top-of-funnel" :description "Top of funnel (TOFU) is the awareness stage, where potential buyers first learn about a problem or a company. Learn what TOFU content and metrics look like."}
{:name "Total Addressable Market (TAM)" :kind "Glossary" :url "https://www.onegtmlab.dev/glossary/total-addressable-market" :description "Total addressable market (TAM) is the full revenue opportunity for a product. Learn how to size TAM bottom up and how it relates to SAM and SOM."}
